s://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net/uploads/CourseImages/htmlcsscertificationtraining-mobile.png","FooterDetails":null,"SmallBanner":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net/uploads/CourseImages/frontendfoundations-small.jpg","VideoCount":0,"ProjectCount":0,"Duration":"10:00:00","Paths":null},{"Id":484,"Name":"React Course with Project","TagLine":"Master React Development with Project, Labs & Q&A","CourseCount":0,"Url":"/course/react-course","MobileBanner":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net/uploads/CourseImages/reactjscourse-mobile.png","FooterDetails":null,"SmallBanner":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net/uploads/CourseImages/reacttsxcourse-small.jpg","VideoCount":0,"ProjectCount":1,"Duration":"02:21:21","Paths":null}]};var json_main_menu={};var sandbox_menu=[{"Id":4,"Name":"AWS AI Cloud Sandbox","Description":"<h3>AWS Cloud Sandbox – Overview</h3><p>The ScholarHat AWS Cloud Sandbox offers a fully isolated and secure environment for hands-on learning and experimentation with Amazon Web Services. Whether you're working with AWS Lambda, Elastic Beanstalk, Amazon EKS, RDS, or DevOps tools, the sandbox provides complete flexibility to build, test, and deploy applications.</p><h4>Key features include:</h4><ul><li><b>AWS Services Access</b>: Utilize a wide range of AWS developer tools and services including serverless apps, APIs, containers, databases, and CI/CD pipelines.</li><li><b>Full Control</b>: Configure resources and infrastructure to match your specific learning or prototyping needs.</li><li><b>Safe &amp; Isolated</b>: Operate in a dedicated AWS environment without affecting production workloads.</li><li><b>Experiment Freely</b>: Ideal for testing ideas, building prototypes, and gaining real-world experience in a risk-free setting.</li></ul><p>If you're looking to explore the full potential of AWS Developer Services in a secure, flexible, and hands-on environment, the ScholarHat AWS Cloud Sandbox is your go-to platform.</p><br><br><br><h3>AWS Sandbox Guidelines</h3><ul><li><b>AWS Account &amp; Resources</b>: Use the AWS account and resources provided by the sandbox for all activities. Do not attempt to create or use additional AWS accounts.</li><li><b>Session Duration</b>: Resources are available only during the active sandbox session. When the session ends, the sandbox environment, resources, and data may be automatically removed.</li><li><b>Authentication</b>: Follow the authentication method provided by the sandbox platform whenever you start a new sandbox session.</li><li><b>Practice Only</b>: The sandbox is intended only for learning, practice, and experimentation. Do not use it for production workloads or business-critical applications.</li><li><b>Limited Permissions</b>: Access is limited to the AWS services, resources, regions, and operations enabled for the sandbox. Some AWS features may not be available.</li><li><b>Quotas &amp; Regions</b>: Resource creation may be subject to service quotas, resource limits, account restrictions, and supported-region restrictions. Use only the AWS regions and resources available in the sandbox.</li><li><b>Resource Limits</b>: Use AWS resources responsibly and create only the resources required for the lab or learning activity. Avoid unnecessary resource consumption.</li><li><b>Session Reset</b>: Each new session may start with a fresh environment. Resources, configurations, and data from previous sessions may not be available.</li></ul><p><b>Important:</b> These limitations help us optimize costs and provide a safe, controlled, and affordable environment for hands-on AWS practice.</p><br>","SandboxConfig":null,"IsActive":null,"CreatedDate":null,"MetaDescription":"AWS Cloud Sandbox","MetaKeyword":"AWS Cloud Sandbox","Url":"/sandbox/aws-ai","Title":"AWS AI Cloud Sandbox","VideoUrl":null,"Logo":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net/article/120261103115557.png","CategoryID":0,"CategoryName":null,"CourseName":null,"HelpUrl":"/user/support/instruction/aws","TroubleshootingUrl":"/user/support/troubleshoot/aws","AccessUrl":"https://099814429382.signin.aws.amazon.com/console","CourseId":null,"CourseType":0,"ExpiryDate":null,"MaxDuration":null},{"Id":3,"Name":"AWS Cloud Sandbox","Description":"<h3>AWS Cloud Sandbox – Overview</h3><p>The ScholarHat AWS Cloud Sandbox offers a fully isolated and secure environment for hands-on learning and experimentation with Amazon Web Services. Whether you're working with AWS Lambda, Elastic Beanstalk, Amazon EKS, RDS, or DevOps tools, the sandbox provides complete flexibility to build, test, and deploy applications.</p><h4>Key features include:</h4><ul><li><b>AWS Services Access</b>: Utilize a wide range of AWS developer tools and services including serverless apps, APIs, containers, databases, and CI/CD pipelines.</li><li><b>Full Control</b>: Configure resources and infrastructure to match your specific learning or prototyping needs.</li><li><b>Safe &amp; Isolated</b>: Operate in a dedicated AWS environment without affecting production workloads.</li><li><b>Experiment Freely</b>: Ideal for testing ideas, building prototypes, and gaining real-world experience in a risk-free setting.</li></ul><p>If you're looking to explore the full potential of AWS Developer Services in a secure, flexible, and hands-on environment, the ScholarHat AWS Cloud Sandbox is your go-to platform.</p><br><br><br><h3>AWS Sandbox Guidelines</h3><ul><li><b>AWS Account &amp; Resources</b>: Use the AWS account and resources provided by the sandbox for all activities. Do not attempt to create or use additional AWS accounts.</li><li><b>Session Duration</b>: Resources are available only during the active sandbox session. When the session ends, the sandbox environment, resources, and data may be automatically removed.</li><li><b>Authentication</b>: Follow the authentication method provided by the sandbox platform whenever you start a new sandbox session.</li><li><b>Practice Only</b>: The sandbox is intended only for learning, practice, and experimentation. Do not use it for production workloads or business-critical applications.</li><li><b>Limited Permissions</b>: Access is limited to the AWS services, resources, regions, and operations enabled for the sandbox. Some AWS features may not be available.</li><li><b>Quotas &amp; Regions</b>: Resource creation may be subject to service quotas, resource limits, account restrictions, and supported-region restrictions. Use only the AWS regions and resources available in the sandbox.</li><li><b>Resource Limits</b>: Use AWS resources responsibly and create only the resources required for the lab or learning activity. Avoid unnecessary resource consumption.</li><li><b>Session Reset</b>: Each new session may start with a fresh environment. Resources, configurations, and data from previous sessions may not be available.</li></ul><p><b>Important:</b> These limitations help us optimize costs and provide a safe, controlled, and affordable environment for hands-on AWS practice.</p><br>","SandboxConfig":null,"IsActive":null,"CreatedDate":null,"MetaDescription":"AWS Cloud Sandbox","MetaKeyword":"AWS Cloud Sandbox","Url":"/sandbox/aws","Title":"AWS Cloud Sandbox","VideoUrl":null,"Logo":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net/article/120261103120218.png","CategoryID":0,"CategoryName":null,"CourseName":null,"HelpUrl":"/user/support/instruction/aws","TroubleshootingUrl":"/user/support/troubleshoot/aws","AccessUrl":"https://099814429382.signin.aws.amazon.com/console","CourseId":null,"CourseType":0,"ExpiryDate":null,"MaxDuration":null},{"Id":1,"Name":"Azure AI Cloud Sandbox","Description":"<h3>Azure AI Cloud Sandbox – Overview</h3><p>The <strong>ScholarHat Azure AI Cloud Sandbox</strong> offers a fully isolated and secure environment for hands-on learning and experimentation with Microsoft Azure AI services. Whether you're exploring <strong>Azure OpenAI</strong>, <strong>Azure AI Foundry</strong>, <strong>Computer Vision</strong>, or <strong>Azure AI Search</strong>, the sandbox provides full freedom to create, manage, and test services.</p><h4>Key features include:</h4><ul><li><b>AI Services Access</b>: Deploy and experiment with any number of Azure AI services.</li><li><b>Full Control</b>: Configure resources and hardware to match your specific learning or prototyping needs.</li><li><b>Safe &amp; Isolated</b>: Operate in a dedicated Azure environment without affecting production workloads.</li><li><b>Experiment Freely</b>: Ideal for testing ideas, building prototypes, and gaining real-world experience in a risk-free setting.</li></ul><p>If you're looking to explore the full potential of Azure AI in a controlled and flexible environment, the ScholarHat Azure AI Cloud Sandbox is your ideal platform.</p><br><br><h3>Azure AI Sandbox Guidelines</h3><ul><li><b>Resource Group</b>: A default resource group is automatically created. You cannot create a new resource group. Use the provided resource group for all Azure AI activities.</li><li><b>Session Duration</b>: Azure AI resources are available only during the active sandbox session. When the session ends, the environment, resources, and data are automatically removed.</li><li><b>Microsoft Authenticator</b>: You must use the Microsoft Authenticator app to authenticate each time you start a new sandbox session.</li><li><b>Practice Only</b>: The sandbox is intended only for learning, experimentation, and practice. Do not use it for production AI workloads or business-critical applications.</li><li><b>Limited Permissions</b>: Access is limited to the Azure AI services, resources, regions, models, and operations enabled for the sandbox. Some Azure AI features may not be available.</li><li><b>Quotas &amp; Regions</b>: AI resource creation and model usage may be subject to quotas, size, quantity, capacity, and region restrictions. Use only the supported Azure regions and available quotas.</li><li><b>AI Model Usage</b>: Access to AI models and services may be limited by the sandbox configuration, available capacity, usage limits, or supported deployments.</li><li><b>Session Reset</b>: Each new session starts with a fresh environment. Azure AI resources, model deployments, configurations, and data from previous sessions will not be available.</li></ul><p><b>Important:</b> These limitations help us optimize costs and provide a safe, controlled, and affordable environment for hands-on Azure AI practice.</p><br>","SandboxConfig":null,"IsActive":null,"CreatedDate":null,"MetaDescription":"Azure AI Cloud Sandbox","MetaKeyword":"Azure AI Cloud Sandbox","Url":"/sandbox/azure-ai","Title":"Azure AI Cloud Sandbox","VideoUrl":null,"Logo":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net/article/120250604115443.png","CategoryID":0,"CategoryName":null,"CourseName":null,"HelpUrl":"/user/support/instruction/azure","TroubleshootingUrl":"/user/support/troubleshoot/azure","AccessUrl":"https://portal.azure.com/","CourseId":null,"CourseType":0,"ExpiryDate":null,"MaxDuration":null},{"Id":2,"Name":"Azure Cloud Sandbox","Description":"<h3>Azure Cloud Sandbox – Overview</h3><p>The ScholarHat Azure Cloud Sandbox offers a fully isolated and secure environment for hands-on learning and experimentation with Microsoft Azure Developer Services. Whether you're working with Azure App Services, Functions, Azure Kubernetes Service, Azure SQL, or DevOps tools, the sandbox provides complete flexibility to build, test, and deploy applications.</p><h4>Key features include:</h4><ul><li><b>Azure Services Access</b>: Utilize a wide range of Azure developer tools and services including web apps, APIs, containers, databases, and CI/CD pipelines..</li><li><b>Full Control</b>: Configure resources and hardware to match your specific learning or prototyping needs.</li><li><b>Safe &amp; Isolated</b>: Operate in a dedicated Azure environment without affecting production workloads.</li><li><b>Experiment Freely</b>: Ideal for testing ideas, building prototypes, and gaining real-world experience in a risk-free setting.</li></ul><p>If you're looking to explore the full potential of Azure Developer Services in a secure, flexible, and hands-on environment, the ScholarHat Azure Cloud Sandbox is your go-to platform.</p><br><br><h3>Azure Sandbox Guidelines</h3><ul><li><b>Resource Group</b>: A default resource group is automatically created. You cannot create a new resource group. Use the provided resource group for all activities.</li><li><b>Session Duration</b>: Resources are available only during the active session. When the session ends, the environment, resources, and data are automatically removed.</li><li><b>Microsoft Authenticator</b>: You must use the Microsoft Authenticator app to authenticate each time you start a new sandbox session.</li><li><b>Practice Only</b>: The sandbox is intended only for learning and practice. Do not use it for production workloads.</li><li><b>Limited Permissions</b>: Access is limited to the services, resources, regions, and operations enabled for the sandbox. Some Azure features may not be available.</li><li><b>Quotas &amp; Regions</b>: Resource creation may be subject to size, quantity, and region restrictions. Use only the supported Azure regions and available quotas.</li><li><b>Session Reset</b>: Each new session starts with a fresh environment. Resources and configurations from previous sessions will not be available.</li></ul><p><b>Important:</b> These limitations help us optimize costs and provide a safe, controlled, and affordable environment for hands-on practice.</p><br>","SandboxConfig":null,"IsActive":null,"CreatedDate":null,"MetaDescription":"Azure Cloud Sandbox","MetaKeyword":"Azure Cloud Sandbox","Url":"/sandbox/azure","Title":"Azure Cloud Sandbox","VideoUrl":null,"Logo":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net/article/120250626121623.png","CategoryID":0,"CategoryName":null,"CourseName":null,"HelpUrl":"/user/support/instruction/azure","TroubleshootingUrl":"/user/support/troubleshoot/azure","AccessUrl":"https://portal.azure.com/","CourseId":null,"CourseType":0,"ExpiryDate":null,"MaxDuration":null}];var skill_categories=[{"CourseCategoryId":42,"CourseCategoryName":".NET Platform","Description":null,"CreatedDate":null,"UpdatedDate":null,"DomainName":null,"IsActive":false,"CurType":11,"CourseCount":0,"MobileBanner":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net/uploads/CourseImages/netplatform-mobile.png","Mobile":null,"CourseMenu":[{"Id":262,"Name":"Building REST API Using Express, MongoDB & Design Patterns","TagLine":null,"CourseCount":0,"Url":"/courses/nodejs/building-rest-api-express-mongodb","MobileBanner":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net","FooterDetails":"<ul class=\"ul-bullet-dark\"><li>Operating System: Windows 7+, Mac OS X, or Ubuntu</li><li>SDK and IDE: Node.js, VS Code</li><li>Database: MongoDB and MongoDB Compass</li><li>Web Browser: Firefox or Chrome or Opera or Microsoft Edge</li><li>Internet Connectivity</li></ul>","SmallBanner":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net/uploads/CourseImages/buildingrestapiusingexpressmongodbdesignpatterns-small.jpg","VideoCount":18,"ProjectCount":null,"Duration":"02:22:03","Paths":null},{"Id":280,"Name":"C# Arrays and Strings","TagLine":null,"CourseCount":0,"Url":"/courses/csharp/arrays-strings","MobileBanner":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net","FooterDetails":"<ul class=\"ul-bullet-dark\"><li>Operating System: Windows 7 or Higher</li>\r\n<li>SDK: .NET 4.5, .NET Core</li><li>IDE : Visual Studio 2017 or Higher</li>\r\n</ul>","SmallBanner":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net","VideoCount":9,"ProjectCount":null,"Duration":"00:46:23","Paths":null},{"Id":278,"Name":"C# Concepts: Anonymous Type, Delegates, Events and Lambda","TagLine":null,"CourseCount":0,"Url":"/courses/csharp/anonymous-type-delegates-events-lambda-expression","MobileBanner":"https://dotnettrickscloud.blob.core.windows.net/uploads/CourseImages/cconceptsanonymoustypedelegate